<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH MAY PPI UP 0.1 PCT MO/MO, 4.1 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>CZECH MAY PPI UP 0.1 PCT MO/MO, 4.1 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech producer prices were 0.1 percent higher in May, putting industrial prices 4.1 percent higher than in the same month on 1996, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>  CZECH PRODUCER PRICES    MAY 1997  APRIL 1997  MAY 1996</p>
<p>Industrial</p>
<p>  pct change month/month     0.1	  0.3	  0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	 4.1	  4.3	  5.1</p>
<p>Construction prices</p>
<p>  pct change month/month     0.8	  1.0	  0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	11.0	 11.1	 10.2</p>
<p>Agricultural prices</p>
<p>  pct change month/month     n/a	  n/a	  n/a</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	-0.7	  0.0	  5.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Construction figures are based on estimates. All figures are in real, inflation-adjusted terms.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
